{{also|Machen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|-}}, from {{inh|de|goh|mahhōn}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*makōn}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*mag-|t=to knead, mix, make}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈmaxən/|[ˈmäχən]|[ˈmäχn̩]|[ˈmäxɛn]|[ˈmɑχən]}}
* {{a|Germany}} {{audio|de|De-machen.ogg}}
* {{a|Austria|Southern Germany}} {{audio|de|De-at-machen.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|de|aχən|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[make]], [[produce]], [[create]] (an object, arrangement, situation, etc.)
#: {{uxi|de|Ich '''hab''' dir einen Kuchen '''gemacht'''!|I '''made''' you a pie!}}
#: {{uxi|de|Du hast einen Fehler '''gemacht'''.|You '''made''' a mistake.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|of food, drinks, etc.}} to make, [[prepare]]
#: {{uxi|de|'''Machst''' du heute das Essen?|'''Are''' you '''making''' dinner today?}}
#: {{uxi|de|sich eine Pizza '''machen'''|to '''prepare''' a pizza for oneself}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|informal}} to [[do]], [[perform]], [[carry out]] {{gloss|to execute; to put into operation (an action)}}
#: {{uxi|de|'''Mach''' es!|'''Do''' it!}}
#: {{uxi|de|Das '''hat''' er ganz allein '''gemacht'''!|He '''did''' that all by himself!}}
#: {{uxi|de|ein Experiment '''machen'''|to '''perform''' an experiment}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|with a noun}} to [[do]]; {{n-g|indicates an activity associated with a noun}}
#: {{uxi|de|Sport '''machen'''|'''do''' sports}}
#: {{uxi|de|eine Party '''machen'''|'''have''' a party}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[go]] {{gloss|to make the (specified) sound}}
#: {{uxi|de|Das Auto '''machte''' "Bumm" und hielt an.|The car '''went''' "boom" and stopped.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[make]] {{gloss|to cause or compel (to do something)}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|of difficulties, pain, etc.}} to [[cause]] {{gloss|to set off an event or action or produce as a result}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|with an adjective}} to [[make]] {{gloss|to cause to be}}
#: {{uxi|de|Dieser Film '''macht''' mich schläfrig.|This '''movie''' makes me sleepy.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|with a noun}} to [[make]] {{gloss|transform from one thing into another}}
#: {{uxi|de|Die Mühle '''macht''' Mehl aus Weizen.|The mill '''makes''' flour from wheat.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|usually not translated literally}} to [[make]] {{gloss|to have as a feature}}
#: {{uxi|de|Die Straße '''macht''' vor uns eine Linkskurve.|The road '''makes''' a turn to the left ahead.}}
<!--Collins gives the example: "die Straße macht einen Knick" with the example "the road bends"-->
# {{lb|de|transitive|informal|colloquial}} to [[come to]], [[total]], [[cost]] {{gloss|to require the payment of}}
#: {{uxi|de|Wie viel '''macht''' das?|How much '''does''' that '''come to'''?}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|arithmetic}} to [[make]], [[be]] {{gloss|the result of a calculation}}
#: {{uxi|de|Sieben plus fünf '''macht''' zwölf.|Seven plus five '''makes''' twelve.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|informal|colloquial}} to [[make]] {{gloss|to earn, gain wages, profit, etc.}}
#: {{ux|de|Der Herr Müller ist echt reich; der '''macht''' mehr als 5000 Euro im Monat.|Mr Müller is quite rich; he '''makes''' more than 5000 Euros per month.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[be]], [[play]] {{gloss|to act as the indicated role, especially in a performance}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|impersonal|colloquial}} to [[matter]] {{gloss|to be important}}
#: {{uxi|de|Das '''macht''' nichts!|That doesn't '''matter'''!}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[make]], make oneself out to be, [[act]], [[play]] {{gloss|to behave so as to give an appearance of being; to act as if one were (something, or a certain way)}} {{+preo|de|auf}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|informal|euphemistic}} to [[do one's business]], do [[number two]] or [[number one]], [[go]] {{gloss|to defecate or urinate}}
#: {{uxi|de|{{q|childish}} groß '''machen'''|'''to go''' poop}}
#: {{uxi|de|{{q|childish}} klein '''machen'''|'''to go''' pee}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[do]] {{gloss|to fare or perform (well or poorly)}}
#: {{uxi|de|'''Machen''' Sie sich gut?|Are you '''doing''' well?}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive}} to [[look]] {{gloss|to have an appearance of being}}
#: {{uxi|de|Der Mantel '''macht''' sich sehr schön.|The coat '''looks''' very nice.}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive|_|dative|colloquial}} to [[get cracking]] ({{m|de|an}} (“on,” “with”)), [[get a move on]] (it), to [[get down]] ({{m|de|an}} (“to”)) (something); {{q|in imperative:}} [[come on]], [[let's go]]

====Usage notes====
*Unlike the English distinction between ''make'' and ''do'', the verb {{m|de|machen|t=[[make]]}} can be used as a synonym for {{m|de|tun|t=[[do]]}} in most cases. However, ''tun'' cannot be used for the proper senses of ''machen''.
*The verb ''machen'' can be combined with many different nouns to create various expressions. These can often be translated into English with [[make]] or [[take]]. For many of these expressions, a more specific verb is available and is usually preferred in formal or written language.
*: {{uxi|de|Angaben machen|to provide information}}
*: {{uxi|de|eine Aufzeichnung machen|to keep a record}}
*: {{uxi|de|Ausflüchte machen|to make excuses}}
*: {{uxi|de|Bankrott/Pleite machen|to go bankrupt}}
*: {{uxi|de|eine Besorgung machen|to run an errand}}
*: {{uxi|de|ein Bett machen|to make a bed}}
*: {{uxi|de|Feierabend machen|to call it a day}}
*: {{uxi|de|Ferien machen|to take a vacation, to go on holiday}}
*: {{uxi|de|ein Feuer machen|to light a fire}}
*: {{uxi|de|ein Foto machen|to take a picture}}
*: {{uxi|de|Fortschritte machen|to make headway}}
*: {{uxi|de|Gewinn machen|to turn a profit}}
*: {{uxi|de|Kasse machen|to cash in}}
*: {{uxi|de|einen Krach machen|to make a racket}}
*: {{uxi|de|Notizen machen|to take notes}}
*: {{uxi|de|Platz machen|to make room}}
*: {{uxi|de|eine Reise machen|to take a trip}}
*: {{uxi|de|Schluss machen|to call it quits}}
*: {{uxi|de|Spaß machen|to be fun}}
*: {{uxi|de|Überstunden machen|to do overtime}}
*: {{uxi|de|Witze machen|to joke}}

